KeywordAbility(
    name: "offspring",
    params: [Cost],
    spelling: "offspring <Param(0)>",
    grammar: FixedKeyword(
        surface: "offspring",
    ),
    // UNBODIED, not blocked. "Offspring [cost]" means "You may pay an additional
    // [cost] as you cast this spell" and "When this permanent enters, if its
    // offspring cost was paid, create a token that's a copy of it, except it's
    // 1/1." [CR#702.175a] Both halves are writable — `StaticSpec::AddedCost` and an
    // enters trigger reading `Paid(Readback(ByKeyword("Offspring")))` — and since
    // `lean-keyword-definition-regimes` each is checked against its own regime (the
    // cost at casting, the trigger off the stack). The body is owed to
    // `semantics-v2-keyword-ability-residues`.
)
